<!-- PHILOSOPHY -->
<strong>Philosophy</strong>
<ul>
  <li>What is life and what is the purpose of it, and why do we even exist?</li>
  <li>Does God exist?</li>

  <li>Nothing & Something:
    <ul>
      <li>What is nothing?</li>
      <li>What is something?</li>
      <li>Can something come from nothing?</li>
      <li>How can something come from nothing?</li>
      <li>Why is there anything at all instead of nothing?</li>
      <li>If energy can neither be created nor destroyed, how does this energy exist?</li>
      <li>How could the universe come from nothing?</li>
      <li>How did "nothing" exist before the Big Bang?</li>
      <li>How did the Big Bang happen from nothing?</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li>Determinism, fatalism, and free will</li>

  <li>Free will vs determinism:
    <ul>
      <li>Compatibilism (soft determinism)</li>
      <li>Incompatibilism
        <ul>
          <li>Libertarianism</li>
          <li>Hard determinism</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li>What is truth, really—and how do we know what’s true?
    <ul>
      <li>Can human beings ever fully understand truth or reality?</li>
      <li>What is reality itself—does it exist independently of perception?</li>
      <li>Is truth something we discover, or something we construct?</li>
      <li>What is reality before or after truth?</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li>What’s right and wrong? What's fair and unfair?</li>
  <li>Is morality subjective?</li>

  <li>Are humans inherently good or evil? Are people born evil?
    <ul>
      <li>The psychology of people who commit crimes</li>
    </ul>
  </li>

  <li>Who am I? What is the self?</li>
  <li>Is mathematics discovered or invented?</li>
  <li>What happens after we die?</li>
  <li>Is antinatalism justified?</li>
</ul>

